        0 & \text{if } \text{input}_{i} = 0.0 \text{ and } \text{other}_{i} != \text{NaN} \\
        \text{input}_{i} * \text{log1p}(\text{other}_{i})& \text{otherwise}
    \end{cases}

Similar to SciPy's `scipy.special.xlog1py`.



Args:
